## Ready-made files, regenerated on every update

| File | What it gives you |
|---|---|
| [`opencode.json`](opencode.json) | Drop-in [opencode](https://opencode.ai) config with every provider wired up — keys via `{env:...}`, keyless endpoints work immediately; a lane that wants a session header per conversation is left out of both generated configs, and its row above names the header |
| [`free-llm.env.example`](free-llm.env.example) | Commented env exports for any OpenAI-compatible tool |
| [`claude-code.sh`](claude-code.sh) | One shell function per gateway that serves the Anthropic Messages format — `source` it and {% if claude_example %}`{{ claude_example }}` runs [Claude Code](https://code.claude.com/docs) on that lane{% else %}run the function named after a row to start [Claude Code](https://code.claude.com/docs) on its lane{% endif %}, key and model filled in where the row lists one |
| [`litellm.yaml`](litellm.yaml) | [LiteLLM](https://docs.litellm.ai) proxy config: `litellm --config configs/litellm.yaml --host 127.0.0.1` puts every free model LiteLLM can call behind one local endpoint{% if litellm_groups %}. Ask for {{ litellm_groups | either_code }} instead of a model and a call moves to the next free lane when one runs out of quota or has no key set{% endif %} — without `--host` the proxy listens on every interface, and the file sets no master key |
| [`../llms.txt`](../llms.txt) | The whole list as one text file for LLM search and agents — every live offer with its page, what it needs (card, key) and where it answers — [served on the site]({{ pages_url }}/llms.txt) |
| [`../index.json`](../index.json) | Machine-readable registry: `curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mvalentsev/awesome-free-ai-coding/main/index.json \| jq '.entries[].id'` |
| [`../history.jsonl`](../history.jsonl) · [feed]({{ feed_url }}) | Append-only log of every change to the list — one JSON object per line, and the same thing as an Atom feed your reader can subscribe to |
| [`browse.html`]({{ pages_url }}/browse.html) | The list as a filterable table — category, no card, no key, OpenAI-compatible, Claude Code route, frontier models — reading `index.json` in the browser |
| [provider pages]({{ pages_url }}/providers/) | One page per row — the free tier in the vendor's own words, the connection details, the evidence the probe reads and the row's history |
